# .dockerignore — mosko-fintech repo root
#
# Excludes paths from Docker build contexts that use the repo root as the build
# context. The V1 web-app and PDF worker containers are the V1 build targets
# (per ARCH §5 + ARCH §2 Components); both inherit this exclusion list.
#
# Per-container Dockerfiles may also carry container-scoped .dockerignore files
# under their respective directories (e.g., workers/pdf-render/.dockerignore).

# CI fence golden-test fixtures (Phase 5 Step 4 W1) — MUST stay out of production
# build contexts per Sec rubric (b)3 #2. Fixtures are deliberately violation-shaped
# (raw psycopg2.connect outside TenantBoundConnection class; out-of-allowlist
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY reference; Dockerfile with Postgres client install).
# If accidentally bundled into a production image, the TBC fixture would be a real
# security hazard (runtime-loadable raw connection).
tests/

# Working artifacts + meta-process scratch (per feedback_working_artifacts_temp_not_docs).
temp/

# VCS + IDE artifacts.
.git/
.github/
.husky/
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# Node — handled per-container but defensively excluded at root.
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Python — handled per-container but defensively excluded at root.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/

# Documentation + planning artifacts — not needed in any production container.
docs/
*.md
!CLAUDE.md  # keep per-directory CLAUDE.md instructions visible at debug time
